user_prompt:
Assemble the final lossless remittance package that can generate an 835 with no loss relative to the provided text and with complete traceability, combining: the X12 835 AST, the semantic model, the enrichment context + completion policy, the integrity outcome, and immutable raw-text evidence references. This is the final publish stage — do NOT alter the X12 model, only package and finalize it for export.

Source-of-truth policy: reply.x12 is the single source of truth for serialization; reply.semantic is for UI/analytics only.

Preservation rules: always include semantic.unmapped_text; always include the E4 completion policy that was used; if duplicates were removed upstream, that must remain visible in provenance or warnings.

Provenance assembly: merge remit_canonical_package.provenance.field_origins, remit_context_package.provenance.enriched_fields, and x12_model_package.segment_provenance into reply.provenance, normalizing each record's source to one of text | payer_master | payee_master | system_config | synthetic_policy | computed, with evidence_refs limited to E1 anchors only.

Missing inputs and warnings: take the union of remit_canonical_package.missing_inputs, remit_context_package.missing_inputs, and any integrity_outcome_package findings/warnings that recommend needs_more_input; de-duplicate.

Hashing: compute hashes.sha256_raw_text (from the E1 package if provided, else carried through from canonicalizer provenance), hashes.sha256_x12_model (canonical serialization of the x12 model JSON), and hashes.sha256_reply (canonical serialization of the reply JSON). Canonical serialization = stable key ordering, UTF-8, no whitespace.

If include_evidence_index is not requested, do not embed any raw text or E1 line index content in the reply (default should minimize PHI exposure).

If the integrity outcome status is FAIL: still emit a complete package, but set reply.integrity.status="FAIL", include the findings, and add a warning emphasizing the package is "not safe to ingest".

Validations you must satisfy: (V1) reply.x12.transactions must contain at least one 835 transaction with ST/SE; (V2) reply.integrity.status must equal the integrity_outcome_package status exactly; (V3) never change any upstream semantic or x12 content — only reference/copy it; (V4) every required top-level field must be present.

Return ONLY this JSON object (no markdown, no extra text):
{
  "document_id": "doc_...",
  "package_type": "lossless_835_package",
  "package_version": "1.0.0",
  "reply": {
    "x12": {
      "profile": {
        "implementation_version": "005010X221A1",
        "delimiters": {
          "element": "*",
          "segment": "~",
          "component": ":"
        }
      },
      "envelope": {},
      "transactions": []
    },
    "semantic": {
      "header": {},
      "claims": [],
      "unmapped_text": []
    },
    "context": {
      "payer_context": {},
      "payee_context": {},
      "x12_profile": {},
      "completion_policy": {}
    },
    "integrity": {
      "status": "PASS|REVIEW|FAIL",
      "summary": {},
      "findings": []
    },
    "provenance": {
      "field_origins": [],
      "segment_provenance": [],
      "policy_id": "",
      "policy_version": ""
    },
    "missing_inputs": [],
    "warnings": []
  },
  "hashes": {
    "sha256_raw_text": "",
    "sha256_x12_model": "",
    "sha256_reply": ""
  },
  "errors": []
}

